('Max Freq Stack','MaxFreqStack supports push, pop that removes the most frequent element (ties broken by recency). Implementation uses:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["Single priority queue","Map of frequency to stack + freq map + maxFreq tracker — all O(1)","Sorted linked list","Binary heap only"]','Map of frequency to stack + freq map + maxFreq tracker — all O(1)'),
('Trapping Rain Stack','Trapping Rain Water using a stack: pop when current height > stack top to compute trapped water. Time:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["O(n^2)","O(n log n)","O(n)","O(n^3)"]','O(n)'),
('Maximal Rect','Maximal rectangle in binary matrix: computed in O(m*n) by applying:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["2D DP only","Largest Rectangle in Histogram for each row using stack","BFS","DFS"]','Largest Rectangle in Histogram for each row using stack'),
('Remove Dup Letters','Remove Duplicate Letters (result is smallest lexicographic subsequence with all chars once). Algorithm?','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["Sort then deduplicate","Greedy monotonic stack: pop larger char if it appears later, push current","BFS","Backtracking"]','Greedy monotonic stack: pop larger char if it appears later, push current'),
('Flatten Nested','Flatten nested list iterator uses a stack where:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["All integers are pre-extracted","List of NestedIntegers is pushed; on next(), flatten from stack top until integer is found","BFS queue","Recursion only"]','List of NestedIntegers is pushed; on next(), flatten from stack top until integer is found'),
('Online Stock Span','Online Stock Span merges consecutive days with lower or equal price. Stack stores (price,span) pairs. Each price is processed:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["O(n) per element worst case","Amortized O(1) — each price pushed and popped at most once","O(log n) with binary search","O(n^2) total"]','Amortized O(1) — each price pushed and popped at most once'),
('Car Fleet','Car Fleet problem: fleet forms when a slower car catches up. Stack approach processes cars sorted by position, storing travel times. Complexity?','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["O(n^2)","O(n log n) — dominated by sort","O(n)","O(n log^2 n)"]','O(n log n) — dominated by sort'),
('Exclusive Time Func','Exclusive time of functions using a log of start/end events uses a stack to track:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["All completed functions","Currently running function — on end, add elapsed time to its exclusive time","Return values","Function pointers"]','Currently running function — on end, add elapsed time to its exclusive time'),
('Robot Seq','Daily Temperatures: find days until a warmer day. Uses:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["Two pointer","Monotonic decreasing stack of indices — O(n)","Sorting","Binary search per element"]','Monotonic decreasing stack of indices — O(n)'),
('132 Stack Solution','132 Pattern detection: scanning right to left, the stack stores candidates for the third element (k). A variable tracks:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["The minimum so far","The best (largest) third element found below the last popped element (s3)","The middle element","All candidates"]','The best (largest) third element found below the last popped element (s3)'),
('Stack Sortable','A sequence is stack-sortable if it can be sorted using a single stack with push/pop operations to output in sorted order. This is equivalent to the sequence containing no ___ pattern.','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["123","132","213","231"]','231'),
('Iterative InOrder','Iterative in-order traversal of BST uses a stack: push left spine, then on pop:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["Recurse right","Process node, then push right subtree''s left spine","Pop again","Use queue for right"]','Process node, then push right subtree''s left spine'),
('Ceil Stack','Given a stack with natural numbers, to implement a ceil operation (find smallest element >= x) in O(n):','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["Sort the stack","Pop until >= x is found, track answer, then restore — O(n) amortized","Use binary search","Use priority queue"]','Pop until >= x is found, track answer, then restore — O(n) amortized'),
('K Stacks Array','Implement K stacks in a single array of size N efficiently (no wasted space) uses:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["N/K slots each","Free list + top[] + next[] arrays — O(1) push and pop","Sorting","Extra linked list"]','Free list + top[] + next[] arrays — O(1) push and pop'),
('Stack DP','Some DP problems are solved using a stack. The pattern "for each element, combine with previous results while condition holds" is called:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["Memoization","DP with monotonic stack — avoids redundant recomputation","Tabulation","Greedy"]','DP with monotonic stack — avoids redundant recomputation'),
('Infix Complex','Converting complex infix with right-associative operators (like ^) to postfix: right-associative means when same precedence, pop only if:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["Stack top has higher precedence","Stack top has strictly higher precedence (not equal)","Stack top has lower precedence","Stack is empty"]','Stack top has strictly higher precedence (not equal)'),
('Balanced Ternary','A stack of size n can hold at most n elements. Using it to check balanced ternary brackets adds complexity of:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["O(n^2)","O(n)","O(log n)","O(1)"]','O(n)'),
('Stack Interview','Given a stack, to get the bottom element without extra data structures requires:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["Impossible","Recursion: pop all, get last, push back — O(n) space on call stack","Extra variable","Sort the stack"]','Recursion: pop all, get last, push back — O(n) space on call stack'),
('Plate Stack','Plate of stacks: push to last stack if capacity not exceeded, else create new stack. Pop from last stack, remove it if empty. Get peak from any sub-stack uses:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["Single stack","Vector of stacks with O(1) amortized push/pop and O(1) popAt for any index","Linked list of stacks","Priority queue"]','Vector of stacks with O(1) amortized push/pop and O(1) popAt for any index'),
('Weird Stack','A stack that supports push, pop, and getMiddle (middle element) in O(1) can be implemented using:','MCQ','HARD','DSA','Stack','["Two stacks","A doubly linked list with a middle pointer, updated on push/pop","Array with midpoint tracking","Three stacks"]','A doubly linked list with a middle pointer, updated on push/pop'),
-- HARD CODING
('Daily Temperatures','Write C++ dailyTemperatures(vector<int>& t) returning days until warmer using monotonic decreasing stack of indices.','CODING','HARD','DSA','Stack',NULL,'vector<int> dailyTemperatures(vector<int>& t){int n=t.size();vector<int> res(n,0);stack<int> st;for(int i=0;i<n;i++){while(!st.empty()&&t[st.top()]<t[i]){res[st.top()]=i-st.top();st.pop();}st.push(i);}return res;}'),
('Trapping Rain Stack Code','Write C++ trap(vector<int>& h) for Trapping Rain Water using a stack.','CODING','HARD','DSA','Stack',NULL,'int trap(vector<int>& h){int n=h.size(),res=0;stack<int> st;for(int i=0;i<n;i++){while(!st.empty()&&h[st.top()]<h[i]){int bot=st.top();st.pop();if(st.empty())break;int dist=i-st.top()-1;int bounded=min(h[i],h[st.top()])-h[bot];res+=bounded*dist;}st.push(i);}return res;}'),
('Remove Dup Letters Code','Write C++ removeDuplicateLetters(string s) using monotonic greedy stack. Result is smallest lex subsequence with each letter once.','CODING','HARD','DSA','Stack',NULL,'string removeDuplicateLetters(string s){vector<int> cnt(26,0);vector<bool> inStk(26,false);for(char c:s)cnt[c-\'a\']++;stack<char> st;for(char c:s){cnt[c-\'a\']--;if(inStk[c-\'a\'])continue;while(!st.empty()&&st.top()>c&&cnt[st.top()-\'a\']>0){inStk[st.top()-\'a\']=false;st.pop();}st.push(c);inStk[c-\'a\']=true;}string res="";while(!st.empty()){res+=st.top();st.pop();}reverse(res.begin(),res.end());return res;}'),
('Maximal Rectangle Code','Write C++ maximalRectangle(vector<vector<char>>& matrix) using largest-rect-in-histogram approach.','CODING','HARD','DSA','Stack',NULL,'int maximalRectangle(vector<vector<char>>& m){if(m.empty())return 0;int n=m[0].size(),res=0;vector<int> h(n,0);for(auto& row:m){for(int i=0;i<n;i++)h[i]=row[i]==\'1\'?h[i]+1:0;stack<int> st;for(int i=0;i<=n;i++){int cur=i==n?0:h[i];while(!st.empty()&&h[st.top()]>cur){int ht=h[st.top()];st.pop();int w=st.empty()?i:i-st.top()-1;res=max(res,ht*w);}st.push(i);}}return res;}'),
('Basic Calculator Code','Write C++ calculate(string s) for basic calculator (+,-,() no multiply). Use stack to save result and sign on (.','CODING','HARD','DSA','Stack',NULL,'int calculate(string s){stack<int> st;int res=0,sign=1,i=0;while(i<s.size()){char c=s[i];if(isdigit(c)){int num=0;while(i<s.size()&&isdigit(s[i]))num=num*10+(s[i++]-\'0\');res+=sign*num;continue;}else if(c==\'+\')sign=1;else if(c==\'-\')sign=-1;else if(c==\'(\'){st.push(res);st.push(sign);res=0;sign=1;}else if(c==\')\'){res=st.top()*res;st.pop();res+=st.top();st.pop();}i++;}return res;}');

